<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns A rating to IBM's samurai bond.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns A rating to IBM's samurai bond.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's said on Thursday that it had assigned its A rating to International Business Machines Corp's (IBM) 50 billion yen worth of 5.3 percent three-year yen/U.S. dollar dual-currency samurai bonds.</p>
<p>The rating agency has affirmed its A ratings for IBM's corporate credit rating and senior unsecured debt. S&amp;P has also affirmed a single A minus rating for the firm's preferred stock and A1 rating for IBM's commercial paper.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said the outlook of the company was stable.</p>
</text>
